WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:01.820
- We're gonna wrap this hour up

00:00:01.820 --> 00:00:04.535
with one last feel-good story,
This is "What I'm Liking."

00:00:04.535 --> 00:00:07.780
(upbeat music)

00:00:07.780 --> 00:00:10.470
Our final guest of the
day basically grew up

00:00:10.470 --> 00:00:13.620
as one of the stars of the
FX series "Better Things."

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:16.480
When she started the show,
she was actually just nine.

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:20.010
Now, as the show heads into
its fifth, final season,

00:00:20.010 --> 00:00:21.630
she's reflecting back and looking forward,

00:00:21.630 --> 00:00:23.766
so everybody say hello to Olivia Edward!

00:00:23.766 --> 00:00:25.543
(audience claps)

00:00:25.543 --> 00:00:26.461
Hi Olivia!

00:00:26.461 --> 00:00:27.950
- Hi.

00:00:27.950 --> 00:00:29.610
- Oh my gosh, so how are you feeling

00:00:29.610 --> 00:00:30.760
going into the final season?

00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:32.550
You started the show so young.

00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:34.280
- Yeah, I mean, it feels really

00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:36.500
really bittersweet just
because of how much

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:38.990
of a huge part this show
has been in my life.

00:00:38.990 --> 00:00:42.600
I mean, I started when I was
like eight or nine, I'm 15 now.

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:44.620
But I feel very grateful
to have been able to work

00:00:44.620 --> 00:00:47.400
with the entire cast and
crew, especially Pamela Adlon

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:50.060
who not just stars, but
also writes, directs,

00:00:50.060 --> 00:00:51.810
and produces the entire show.

00:00:51.810 --> 00:00:52.970
She's incredible.

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:55.680
I mean, I'm going to be
forever grateful for her,

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:57.500
just for teaching me
everything, not just in acting,

00:00:57.500 --> 00:00:59.330
but also in directing and writing.

00:00:59.330 --> 00:01:01.100
So I'm really excited to,
like the characters do

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:03.490
this season, move forward,
make big decisions about

00:01:03.490 --> 00:01:04.323
what I wanna do,

00:01:04.323 --> 00:01:06.253
and take everything that
I've learned with me.

00:01:06.253 --> 00:01:07.086
- I love that.

00:01:07.086 --> 00:01:07.919
(audience cheers)

00:01:07.919 --> 00:01:10.160
I love that experience
too, as a young woman

00:01:10.160 --> 00:01:12.240
having other women so
supportive around you.

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:13.090
That's really cool.

00:01:13.090 --> 00:01:15.090
I'm glad you got that right off the bat.

00:01:15.090 --> 00:01:16.090
I have to say this

00:01:16.090 --> 00:01:18.160
'cause your dad is psychic
medium John Edwards.

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:22.310
So were you able to get away
with anything as a teenager?

00:01:22.310 --> 00:01:23.410
Oh, you're still a teenager.

00:01:23.410 --> 00:01:24.410
Are you able to get away

00:01:24.410 --> 00:01:25.348
with anything?

00:01:25.348 --> 00:01:26.980
(audience laughs)

00:01:26.980 --> 00:01:28.040
- No, I'm not.

00:01:28.040 --> 00:01:30.240
And honestly, it doesn't even have to be

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:31.270
like a sneaky thing,

00:01:31.270 --> 00:01:32.910
like it can be like a nice thing.

00:01:32.910 --> 00:01:34.710
I tried surprising him with you know,

00:01:34.710 --> 00:01:35.810
like a birthday gift.

00:01:35.810 --> 00:01:36.670
I put it in his closet

00:01:36.670 --> 00:01:37.830
until it was time to take it out.

00:01:37.830 --> 00:01:39.780
And then he comes home,
automatically starts

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:40.640
like asking me questions.

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:42.280
He's like, "Hey, did you
put something in my closet?"

00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:43.113
Hasn't been in there yet.

00:01:43.113 --> 00:01:45.650
And I'm like, "No, why would I,

00:01:45.650 --> 00:01:47.343
no, don't go in the closet.

00:01:47.343 --> 00:01:48.760
" But it's like, you know,

00:01:48.760 --> 00:01:50.460
I can't do any of that stuff.

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:52.640
- I love that you have this
relationship with your dad.

00:01:52.640 --> 00:01:53.980
That's so cool.

00:01:53.980 --> 00:01:54.970
Not everybody has it.

00:01:54.970 --> 00:01:55.803
That's so special.

00:01:55.803 --> 00:01:56.860
I'm so happy for you.

00:01:56.860 --> 00:01:58.390
Especially the women, like I said,

00:01:58.390 --> 00:02:00.360
that are so supportive
early on in your career.

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:01.370
I can't wait to see what you do.

00:02:01.370 --> 00:02:02.901
I mean, you started at
nine you're only 15.

00:02:02.901 --> 00:02:04.030
(audience clapping)

00:02:04.030 --> 00:02:07.150
So, congratulations and thanks,
Olivia, for hanging with us

00:02:07.150 --> 00:02:08.783
I'm liking your post right now, alright?

00:02:08.783 --> 00:02:12.400
(audience cheers)

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:15.140
All right, everybody catch new
episodes of "Better Things"

00:02:15.140 --> 00:02:18.010
Monday nights at 10
Eastern and Pacific on FX

00:02:18.010 --> 00:02:19.580
and streaming on Hulu.

00:02:19.580 --> 00:02:22.880
So usually at this point,
we'd give our guest money

00:02:22.880 --> 00:02:24.760
on behalf of Pilot pen,
makers of "Frixion,"

00:02:24.760 --> 00:02:27.230
the go-to erasable pen of
the Kelly Clarkson Show.

00:02:27.230 --> 00:02:29.280
But today, that thousand dollars is going

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:30.440
to someone in the audience.

00:02:30.440 --> 00:02:31.356
So, look under your chairs!

00:02:31.356 --> 00:02:34.473
(audience cheering)

00:02:34.473 --> 00:02:36.330
Look under your chairs!

00:02:36.330 --> 00:02:38.085
Who's got it?

00:02:38.085 --> 00:02:40.830
Somebody's got it under your chair.

00:02:40.830 --> 00:02:42.040
We've never had an audience

00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:43.977
that...There you go! There you go!

00:02:43.977 --> 00:02:46.810
(audience cheers)

00:02:48.180 --> 00:02:49.040
So wait, what's your name?

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:50.110
Where are you from?
- My name is

00:02:50.110 --> 00:02:51.590
Sandra from San Diego.

00:02:51.590 --> 00:02:53.500
- Sandra from San Diego, San Di-ah-go.

00:02:53.500 --> 00:02:54.370
I love it.

00:02:55.622 --> 00:02:56.455
What are you gonna do

00:02:56.455 --> 00:02:57.288
with your money you think?

00:02:57.288 --> 00:02:59.210
- Well, it's my friend
Sharon's birthday today.

00:02:59.210 --> 00:03:00.460
- [Kelly] Oh.
- So,

00:03:00.460 --> 00:03:01.807
she was really excited to come see you.

00:03:01.807 --> 00:03:03.900
So now I could take
her to lunch too, girl!

00:03:03.900 --> 00:03:05.293
- [Kelly] Exactly! Exactly!

00:03:05.293 --> 00:03:06.126
(audience cheers)

00:03:06.126 --> 00:03:07.364
Well thank y'all for coming!

00:03:07.364 --> 00:03:08.700
- Thank you so much!
- [Kelly] Have a good lunch!

00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:09.764
- [Sandra] Thank you!

